title StarChess · Board input — select and commit

actor "Human" as H
participant "LiveStarChessBoard" as VIEW <<app>>
participant "useBoardInput" as INPUT <<app>>
participant "board/moves.ts\nscMovesFrom" as SCM <<app>>
participant "MatchStore\nmatchReducer" as STORE <<async>>
participant "commands/queue-action.ts\naddScAction" as QACT <<app>>

== 1 · Select — derive highlights ==

H ARROW_MAIN VIEW : taps own piece
VIEW ARROW_MAIN INPUT : ""onSquareClick(from)""
INPUT ARROW_MAIN INPUT : ""occupancyForViewerMoves""\n(player fog — occult unseen enemies)
INPUT ARROW_MAIN SCM : ""scMovesFrom(occultedMap, …)""
SCM ARROW_MAIN INPUT : ""ScMove[]"" — SC-legal under fog info
INPUT ARROW_ERROR INPUT : filter ""dropsAtResolve""\n(enemy-king square burns C)
INPUT ARROW_MAIN STORE : ""SELECT_SQUARE"" + ""SET_LEGAL_DESTS""

== 2 · Commit ==

H ARROW_MAIN VIEW : taps highlighted destination
VIEW ARROW_MAIN INPUT : ""onSquareClick(to)""
opt last-rank pawn — ""promotes"" / gas-stack promote
  INPUT ARROW_OPTIONAL STORE : ""SET_PENDING_PROMOTION""
  note right of INPUT
    PromotionModal; timeout / End may flush queen
    (SUBMIT_TURN).
  end note
end
INPUT ARROW_MAIN STORE : ""QUEUE_ACTION"" classical C
STORE ARROW_MAIN QACT : ""addScAction""
STORE ARROW_MAIN VIEW : snap + intent overlay re-render

note over INPUT, STORE
  Specials (spawn / Charon / Jump / siege / mine / pawnDouble) also
  enter via ""QUEUE_ACTION"" from GasDeploy / targeting modes — same store.
  Queue shape: scfen-queue.puml. Resolve: resolve.puml.
end note
@enduml

@startuml sc-moves-rules
' purpose: Per-piece SC classical legality (verified against board/moves.ts).
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · scMoves — rule table

note as RULES
  <size:14>**SC classical legality, per piece**</size>
  ====
  **pawn** — single push empty; free classical double from the double-step
  band (mid+to empty); diagonal enemy capture **or hostile mine** (the marine
  attacks the mine — see **mines** below); **no en passant**;
  // Marines attack **only** on the front diagonals. The generator therefore
  // never emits a push onto an occupied square — and where **fog** hides the
  // occupant, the intent is still queueable but resolves as a **block**, not a
  // capture: the marine truncates before the blocker (resolve.puml).
  // Band = ""canPawnDoubleStep"" — start rank **and behind it** (rank ≤2 white,
  // ≥7 black), so a marine deployed on its own back rank keeps the double.
  // Sole owner of the rule: movegen, ""isScMoveShape"" and
  // ""rewriteClassicalAfterB"" all read it, or the board offers a double the
  // resolver refuses to land.
  // Promotes on last rank. Gas ""pawnDouble"" is +1 forward (any rank),
  // including onto last rank when a promotion choice is set; may stack with classical.
  ----
  **knight, king** — leap via ""attacksSquare"". King: **no** self-check /
  castling; **may** step adjacent to enemy king (duel — resolve.puml).
  ----
  **bishop, rook, queen** — rays inclusive of first enemy, exclusive of ally.
  ----
  **SIEGED rook** — every square on the cross (same file/rank),
  blockers ignored, own-occupied excluded — ""firesInPlace"";
  enemy-occupied carries that victim, empties carry ""capture: null""
  (resolve shells them — ""shelling"", no death, no occupy;
  no diagonal / area fire). A hostile mine on an empty ray
  square clears in place (mines are not occupancy, so the
  ray runs through it). Vision footprint from ""vision.ts""
  (9×9 vs tank 5×5).
  ----
  **ally on to** — never emitted.
  ----
  **enemy KING on to** — emitted with ""dropsAtResolve""; resolver drops
  (burns C). UI/brain filter; validation accepts (fog path-discovery).
  ----
  **mines** — a hostile mine is a **target**: ""hostileMineOnTo"" is advisory for
  units that already reach the tile, and **legality-bearing** only for the marine
  front diagonal onto an empty mined tile. Sieged cross squares are always
  emitted (an empty mined square clears in place). Pass ""opts.mines"" or the
  board hides the marine shape.
  Resolve (attack → clear → occupy, walk-over death, chase): resolve.puml.
  ----
  **fog** — not filtered in generator; occupancy is a caller parameter.
end note

note as NOTIMPL
  <size:14>**Deliberately NOT implemented**</size>
  ====
  castling · en passant · self-check / pins · checkmate/stalemate ·
  queue-time path-blocker rejection · B/F generation · gas budgeting
end note

note as XREF
  scfen-queue.puml · resolve.puml ·
  _spec/apps/starchess/starchess-mode.puml · match-store.puml
end note

RULES -[hidden]right- NOTIMPL
NOTIMPL -[hidden]down- XREF
@enduml
